meta {
  name: Server shutdown
  type: http
  seq: 14
  tags: [
    danger
  ]
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/server/control
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "action": "shutdown",
    "delaySeconds": 30
  }
}

docs {
  ## Server shutdown

  Schedule a worldserver shutdown after a delay. Tagged `danger`: this stops the local stack.

  - Method and path: `POST /api/v1/server/control`.
  - Body: `action` is `shutdown` or `restart`; `delaySeconds` is required and 1-3600. Use
    `action: "cancel"` (request 09) to abort the timer before it fires.
  - Write gate: `GmApi.AllowWrites = 1`.
  - Server-control gate: `GmApi.AllowServerControl = 1`.
  - Permission: `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_SERVER_SHUTDOWN_CANCEL` (735) covers cancel;
    `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_SERVER_SHUTDOWN` (734) covers shutdown/restart.
  - Actor: signed `X-GM-Actor` game account id; must have security above `SEC_PLAYER`.
  - Success: `200` with `{"status":"ok"}`. Audit rows: `pending` then `success`.
  - Failure: `400 bad_request` when `delaySeconds` is missing or out of range, `403`
    `server_control_disabled` or `forbidden`, `500 audit_failed`, `503 world_unavailable`.

  After the timer fires, `worldserver` exits. A restart is only an exit: restart the stack with
  `make start` (local) or the supervisor (test realm). Send `cancel` first when testing this
  request, so the timer never fires.
}
